   "input": "/bin/zsh -c 'cat /var/folders/3g/vf36b0b14wzd0fgsgtdp06h00000gp/T/writing-probe/p-10eb5f1b/948445bc.txt'",
   "output": "Read only the page below. Read no other file, and do not run commands or browse. Answer each question from the page alone. When the page does not say, answer \"Not stated\".\n\n<<<PAGE\n# sackview\n\nSee what\u2019s inside a ZIP archive before you unpack it.\n\nList entry names, compressed sizes, and unpacked sizes. Check the total unpacked size against available disk space before extracting elsewhere.\n\n## Install\n\n```sh\npipx install sackview\n```\n\n## Inspect a ZIP archive\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip\n```\n\nLists the archive\u2019s entries with each entry\u2019s name, compressed size, and unpacked size.\n\n## Find the largest entries\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip --largest 10\n```\n\nShows the ten entries with the largest unpacked sizes, largest first.\n\n## Filter by name\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip --find '*.csv'\n```\n\nShows only entries whose names match the pattern.\n\n## Inspect offline\n\nsackview works offline and sends no archive contents to a service. It never extracts entries or changes the archive.\n\n## Supported format\n\nsackview supports ZIP archives only. Other archive formats produce an unsupported-format message.\nPAGE>>>\n\nQuestions:\n(a) What does sackview show you?\n(b) What command lists the entries in photos.zip?\n(c) Does sackview extract files?\n\nReply with only JSON: {\"a\": \"...\", \"b\": \"...\", \"c\": \"...\"}. Start the answer to (c) with Yes, No, or Not stated.",
